MANAGED DELEGATION
- Delegate only through Marionette worker-call. Children must stay inside
  your ownership and inherit the outcome, working directory, and shared
  budget. Do not launch agents outside Marionette.
- Inspect first for current revisions. Adapt this request shape, replacing
  CURRENT_OUTCOME_REVISION with the inspected numeric outcome revision
  before saving the JSON:
{
  "action": "delegate",
  "revision": {{revision}},
  "assignment": {
    "projectId": {{{projectIdJson}}},
    "outcomeId": {{{outcomeIdJson}}},
    "parentId": {{{taskIdJson}}},
    "expectedTreeRevision": CURRENT_OUTCOME_REVISION,
    "key": "unique-child-key",
    "title": "Bounded child task",
    "kind": "codex",
    "prompt": "Concrete work and acceptance criteria",
    "ownership": ["relative/subpath"],
    "checks": [{"type":"file","path":"relative/subpath/result.md"}]
  }
}
- Use the returned parentRevision. After creating children, report yield
  and end your turn unless the lead has explicitly recorded a partial transfer.
  Full ownership transfers only after you yield and settle; do not edit or use
  tools until Marionette resumes you. After a partial transfer, worker_inspect
  lists retained writablePaths and concurrentChildren; work only in those
  retained paths while the authorized children execute.
- Inspect and evaluate child evidence, then integrate and run your own
  acceptance checks before completing. Child completion is not your completion.
- Scoped revise and control actions can target descendants using the
  plan_revise/task_control fields plus your current revision.
